## 3. Multi-Zone Architecture

### 3.1 Can 1 App Handle 500+ Zones? — Technical Analysis

**YES.** Here's how:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              SINGLE APP ARCHITECTURE             │
│                                                   │
│  ┌──────────┐    User opens app                  │
│  │  Mobile   │ ──→ GPS auto-detects zone         │
│  │   App     │ ──→ Sets `active_region_id`       │
│  │ (React    │ ──→ All API calls include          │
│  │  Native)  │     `region_id` parameter         │
│  └──────────┘                                     │
│       │                                           │
│       ▼                                           │
│  ┌──────────┐                                     │
│  │   API    │  Every query filtered by:          │
│  │  Server  │  WHERE region_id = $user_zone      │
│  │ (Node.js)│                                     │
│  └──────────┘                                     │
│       │                                           │
│       ▼                                           │
│  ┌──────────┐                                     │
│  │PostgreSQL│  500 rows in `regions` table       │
│  │ Database │  All data tagged with region_id    │
│  │          │  Indexes on region_id columns      │
│  └──────────┘                                     │
│                                                   │
│  The app doesn't need 500 copies.                │
│  It's 1 app that FILTERS data per zone.          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

